WHAT: drop `find_package(Qt6LinguistTools REQUIRED)` from library/widgets and
      utils/vpiano, the qt_add_translation() calls that need lrelease, the
      lupdate maintainer targets, and the top-level `update-translations`
      aggregate that gathers them.
WHY:  lrelease and lupdate live in qttools -- a repo plugins/qt does not build
      for the host (its ./host is qtbase plus qtdeclarative; verified: no
      lrelease, no lupdate in host/bin or host/libexec) -- and there is no
      cross-built one to borrow, because they are host tools by definition.
      Three separate things break without the package, which is why this is
      five hunks and not one:
        * find_package fails outright (REQUIRED), twice;
        * qt_add_translation() invokes the Qt6::lrelease imported target, which
          does not exist;
        * the update-*-translations custom targets name Qt6::lupdate, and the
          top-level add_dependencies() on them resolves eagerly -- so merely
          DECLARING them is a configure error, not a build one.
UPSTREAM: not-as-is. Upstream would want this behind an option
      (ENABLE_TRANSLATIONS, defaulting ON) rather than commented out. The
      degradation is bounded and honest: the UI is English only. vpianomain.cpp
      already skips installing translators for the C and English locales, and a
      wk node has no locale to speak of. Building qttools for the host would
      remove the need for this patch entirely.
